-- title:
--   Descent of the period maps to the finite-group quotient tower
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ is a prime number and $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible (`hπ`), $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), residue field of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and absolutely unramified in the sense that $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   Coefficient ring: $Onr$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, subject to the group of hypotheses: completeness for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), maximality of that ideal (`hOnr_max`), residual integrality of every element over $\mathcal O$ (`hOnr_alg`: every $x$ satisfies $p(x) \equiv 0 \bmod \pi$ for some monic $p$ over $\mathcal O$), residual algebraic closedness (`hOnr_closed`: every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$), and the Frobenius congruence $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \bmod \pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Write $\mathcal O_2 :=$ `AlgHom.equalizer (Fr.trans Fr) (AlgHom.id 𝒪 Onr)`, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra $\{y \in Onr : Fr(Fr\,y) = y\}$, and $\mathcal O_{2,n} := \mathcal O_2/(\pi^{n+1})$.
--
--   Determinant valuation: $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is a homomorphism with $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   Group data: $G$ is a group, $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism, $\Gamma \le G$ a subgroup containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix and $vdet(\sigma z) = 2$ (`hcent`) and an element $w$ with $vdet(\sigma w) = 1$ (`hodd`); $\Gamma'$ is a subgroup whose elements are exactly the $x \in \Gamma$ with $vdet(\sigma x)$ even (`hΓ'`). The homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ is the projectivisation of $\sigma$ (`hρ`), and $\rho(\Gamma')$ acts on the vertices of the lattice tree of $\mathcal O$ in $K_0$ with finite vertex stabilisers (`hdisc`) and with finitely many orbits, in the form that some finite set $S$ of vertices meets every orbit (`hcocpt`). The matrix $g_1$ is $\operatorname{diag}(\pi, 1)$ (`hg₁`).
--
--   Mumford tower: $N \le \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ satisfies $N \le \rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`), its trace on $\rho(\Gamma)$ is normal there (`hNnorm`) and its relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ is finite (`hNidx`); $DM$ is a `MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`, that is (the fields being summarised here) a tower of schemes $Z_n$ with structure morphisms $zb_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $zt_n$ forming cartesian reduction squares, $zb_n$ proper and flat, finite subsets contained in affine opens, together with period maps $q_n^{DM}$ sending a Deligne datum over an $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$ to a $B$-point of $Z_n$, compatible with the base, natural in $B$, compatible with the transitions, invariant under twisting by elements of $N$, and subject to the chart open-immersion conditions. Here an object of $\,$`Omega K₀ π`$\,$ over $B$ is a Deligne datum: an assignment to each full lattice $M \subset K_0^2$ of a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$ with invertible quotient, monotone under inclusions of lattices, equivariant for scalar homotheties, and nondegenerate at every prime of $B$; $\,$`DeligneDatum.IsPullback B g P P'`$\,$ says $P'$ assigns to each $M$ the preimage under the base-changed action of $g$ of the submodule $P$ assigns to $g \cdot M$.
--
--   Twisted tower: $X : \mathbb N \to$ `Scheme`, with structure morphisms $xb_n : X n \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$, transitions $xt_n : X n \to X(n+1)$, a finite group $G_2$ acting by automorphisms $a_n$ on each $X n$, projections $pr_1^n : X n \to Z n$ and $pr_2^n : X n \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O_{2,n})$, a homomorphism $\theta : \Gamma \to G_2$, and $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphisms $Fr_2^n$ of $\mathcal O_{2,n}$. The hypotheses on these data are: the reduction squares for $(xt_n, xb_n)$ are cartesian (`hcart`); each $xb_n$ is proper (`hproper`) and flat (`hflat`); finite subsets of $X n$ lie in an affine open (`haff`); the $G_2$-action is over the base (`ha_over`) and commutes with the transitions (`ha_xt`); each square $(pr_1^n, pr_2^n, zb_n, \operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1} \to \mathcal O_{2,n})$ is cartesian, so $X n = Z n \times_{\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})} \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O_{2,n})$ (`hX`); $xb_n$ factors as $pr_1^n$ followed by $zb_n$ (`hxb`); the projections are compatible with the transitions (`hxt₁`, `hxt₂`); $\theta$ is surjective (`hθsurj`) with $\theta \gamma = 1$ exactly when $\rho\gamma \in N$ (`hθker`); $Fr_2^n$ is induced by $Fr$ on $\mathcal O_{2,n}$ (`hFr₂`); for $\gamma \in \Gamma$ the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on the second projection through the power $Fr_2^{-vdet(\sigma\gamma)}$ (`ha_pr₂`); and $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on the first projection through the twist of Deligne data by $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, in the form that if $P, P'$ over $B$ satisfy `DeligneDatum.IsPullback B (σ γ)⁻¹ P P'` and $x : \operatorname{Spec} B \to X n$ has $x$ followed by $pr_1^n$ equal to $q_n^{DM}(P)$, then $x$ followed by $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ and then $pr_1^n$ equals $q_n^{DM}(P')$ (`ha_pr₁`).
--
--   Finally $DQ$ is a `TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`: schemes $Y n$ with structure morphisms $yb_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $yt_n$ forming cartesian reduction squares, $yb_n$ proper and flat, and morphisms $p_n : X n \to Y n$ over the base, compatible with the transitions and with cartesian squares $(xt_n, p_n, p_{n+1}, yt_n)$, invariant under the $G_2$-action, finite, surjective, locally epimorphic, and satisfying a local universal property for $G_2$-invariant morphisms (the remaining fields summarised here).
--
--   Conclusion. There exists a family
--   $$q : \forall\, n,\ \forall\ \mathcal O\text{-algebra } B \text{ with } \pi^{n+1} = 0 \text{ in } B,\quad \bigl((Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B) \times \text{Deligne data over } B\bigr) \longrightarrow \bigl(\operatorname{Spec} B \to Y n\bigr),$$
--   the source being the object at $B$ of `AlgFunctor.prod (AlgFunctor.corep Onr) (Omega K₀ π)`, such that the following six statements hold.
--
--   First (defining equation): for every $n$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $(\pi)^{n+1} = 0$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : Onr \to B$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi_2 : \mathcal O_{2,n} \to B$ with $\psi_2(\bar y) = \psi(y)$ for all $y \in \mathcal O_2$, every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$ and every $x : \operatorname{Spec} B \to X n$ such that $x$ followed by $pr_1^n$ is $q_n^{DM}(P)$ and $x$ followed by $pr_2^n$ is $\operatorname{Spec}(\psi_2)$, one has $q\,n\,B\,(\psi, P) = x$ followed by $p_n$.
--
--   Second (over the base): for all $n$, $B$ and $x$ in the source, $q\,n\,B\,x$ followed by $yb_n$ and then by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O \to \mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathcal O \to B$.
--
--   Third (naturality): for all $n$, all $\mathcal O$-algebras $B, B'$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi : B \to B'$ and every $x$ over $B$, $q\,n\,B'\,(\varphi_* x) = \operatorname{Spec}(\varphi)$ followed by $q\,n\,B\,x$, where $\varphi_*$ is the functorial action on pairs (composition with $\varphi$ on the coefficient map, base change on the Deligne datum).
--
--   Fourth (transitions): for all $n$, $B$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$ and also by $\pi^{n+2}$, and all $x$ over $B$, $q\,(n+1)\,B\,x = q\,n\,B\,x$ followed by $yt_n$.
--
--   Fifth (twisted $\Gamma$-invariance): for all $n$, $B$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and all $x, x'$ over $B$ with `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B (σ γ) x x'` — that is, the first component of $x'$ is obtained from that of $x$ by `frobTwist Onr Fr (- vdet (σ γ))`, the twist attached to that power of $Fr$, and the second components satisfy `DeligneDatum.IsPullback B (σ γ)⁻¹ x.2 x'.2` — one has $q\,n\,B\,x' = q\,n\,B\,x$.
--
--   Sixth (coefficient law): for all $n$, $B$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$, all $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\psi, \psi' : Onr \to B$ agreeing on every $y$ with $Fr(Fr\,y) = y$, and every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, $q\,n\,B\,(\psi, P) = q\,n\,B\,(\psi', P)$; thus $q$ depends on the coefficient homomorphism only through its restriction to $\mathcal O_2$.
--
--   This is the construction, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, of the system of period maps on the quotient tower $Y_n$: the points coming from a coefficient homomorphism on the unramified ring together with a Deligne datum are pushed down from the twisted tower $X_n = Z_n \times \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_{2,n}$ along the finite-group quotient morphisms $p_n$, and the six clauses record the defining equation, the structure laws, invariance under the twisted $\Gamma$-action and dependence on the coefficients only through $\mathcal O_2$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib_of_mumfordTower_of_towerQuotientDatum`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib_of_mumfordTower_of_towerQuotientDatum) in assembling the formal quotient datum for the $p$-adic uniformisation of Shimura curves.
